# Secrets — the agent must not read these
.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# Local data stores
*.db

# Build artifacts and noise
node_modules/
coverage/
dist/

# Control surface — protected, but NOT hidden.
#
# These files cannot go in this list. .bobignore removes a file from the
# agent's reach entirely, and the agent has to READ its own rulebook and mode
# in order to be governed by them: listing them here made the CI canary fail
# with "Access denied: .bob/custom_modes.yaml" and the audit refused to run
# without the Engineering Constitution loaded. Governance that cannot be read
# is not governance.
#
# They are protected by the mechanisms built for it, and those work: rule 06
# forbids touching them, the deterministic CI guard blocks any pull request
# that modifies them (it caught exactly that today, before any model ran), and
# CODEOWNERS requires the owner's review. Protection belongs in the gate, not
# in a blindfold.
